  era: "c. 1200\u20131700 CE \xB7 Section 36 \xB7 Indian Economy Through History \xB7 Across the ages"
  title: Medieval trade
  text: Medieval India exported cotton textiles, indigo, sugar and spices, and imported horses, silver and luxury goods. Cities such as Delhi, Agra, Cambay, Surat and Masulipatnam were busy centres of commerce.
